  "title": "The Day of Eid al-Adha (Qurban)",
  "data": "Ghusl, Eid Prayer & Sacrifice\nBathe on this day (highly recommended).\nOffer [Salat al-Eid](AD4), as described in the acts of Eid al-Fitr. On this day, break your fast after Salat al-Eid and eat from the meat of the sacrificed animals.\nSay the supplications reported for before and after Salat al-Eid.\nThe most important is supplication No. 48 of al-Saheefah al-Kaamelah al-Sajjaadiyyah, which begins with “O Allah, This is a blessed day….”\nAlso say supplication No. 46 of the same book, which begins with “O He Who has mercy upon him whom is not compassionated by the servants”.\nSay [Dua al-Nudbah](E34) (The Supplication of Lamentation).\nOffer a sacrifice, which is to slaughter an animal (confirmedly recommended).",
  "tabs": [
    "Takbirat after Prayers\nAt Mina, say these statements fifteen times immediately after fifteen obligatory prayers, beginning with the Zohr Prayer on the Eid al-Azhaa Day and ending with the Fajr Prayer on the thirteenth of Zilhajj.\nElsewhere, say them ten times instead of fifteen, immediately after ten obligatory prayers, beginning with the Zohr Prayer on the Eid al-Azhaa Day and ending with the Fajr Prayer on the twelfth of Zilhajj.\nAccording to the authentic narration mentioned in al-Kafi, the statements are:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ وَلِلّٰهِ الْحَمْدُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ عَلٰى مَا هَدَانَا اَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ عَلٰى مَا رَزَقَنَا مِنْ بَهِيْمَةِ الْاَنْعَامِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ عَلٰى مَاۤ اَبْلَانَا.\nALLAAHO AKBAR ALLAAHO AKBAR LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBAR ALLAAHO AKBAR WA LILLAAHIL HAMD WAL LAAHO AKBAR A’LAA MAA HADAANAA ALLAAHO AKBAR A’LAA MAA RAZAQANAA MIM BAHEEMATIL AN-A’AME WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE A’LAA MAA ABLAANAA.\nAllah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest. Allah is the Greatest, and for Allah is all praise. Allah is the Greatest for what He has guided us to; Allah is the Greatest for what He has provided for us of grazing livestock; and all praise is for Allah for what He has tested us with [and bestowed upon us].\nIt is recommended to repeat these statements immediately after the obligatory and supererogatory (mustahab / naafelah) prayers as many times as possible."
